 "notes": [
  "foreign_in_india: no dedicated foreign-films page or section was reachable. Data comes from the main 50-row table of 'List of highest-grossing films in India' (columns: Rank | Title | Year | Total gross | Language(s) | Ref.), whose legend says 'Background shading indicates a foreign film.' Only three foreign (English-language) films appear in that top 50; 'rank' is the film's overall rank in India among all films, 'foreign_rank' is its order among foreign films. Basis is India domestic gross (page intro: 'based on domestic box office estimates'); the page does not print net figures and has no distributor column, so distributor is null for all rows. Spider-Man: Brand New Day is printed with an asterisk and is stated in prose to be 'the highest grossing foreign film in India'; the asterisk's exact meaning was not recoverable from the markdown conversion (page also has a 'currently showing in theatres' shading legend).",
  "indian_all_time / indian_by_year: figures are WORLDWIDE gross (column 'Worldwide gross'), not India-only and not net. Where Wikipedia prints a range of estimates, ww_gross_cr holds the low end and ww_gross_cr_high the high end; as_printed holds the verbatim cell (US$ conversions in the by-year table were dropped).",
  "Merged cells: Wikipedia uses rowspan for repeated Language/Year values; the markdown conversion left those cells blank. Blank Language/Year cells were filled with the value of the nearest preceding row in that column (standard rowspan semantics). Affected all-time rows: 2, 4, 7, 9, 12, 13, 14, 16, 17, 20, 22, 26, 27, 28, 29, 33, 34, 35, 41, 42, 44, 45, 48, 49, 50. Affected by-year rows: 2016 (Hindi), 2020 (Hindi), 2022 (Telugu). No numeric value was inferred.",
  "indian_by_year: the language column on that table is headed 'Industry'. Only 2016–2025 are returned as requested (the table itself runs 1940–2026; 2026 is Dhurandhar: The Revenge, Hindi, ₹1,852.44 crore).",
  "hindi_dubbed_south: no 'Highest-grossing Hindi-dubbed South Indian films' (or any dubbed-films) table exists on List_of_highest-grossing_Indian_films, List_of_highest-grossing_Hindi_films, List_of_highest-grossing_South_Indian_films, or List_of_highest-grossing_Telugu_films; candidate standalone pages were not fetchable (cache-only). Returned empty rather than guessed.",
  "The task's request to fetch List_of_highest-grossing_Indian_films 'for each year 2016–2025' was satisfied by one page fetch: the page is a single live article whose 'Highest-grossing films by year' table covers all years; there are no per-year versions of the URL.",
  "Fetches went through WebFetch's small summarizing model against a cached copy of each page (Wikipedia is cache-only in this environment); all-time rows were fetched twice (1–25 with NULL and MERGED markers, 26–50 once) and matched."
 ]
